{# Use zone_info['jobid'] to determine documentation links #}
{% if '-hpc-' in zone_info['jobid'] %}
    {% set doc_base = "https://docs.vscentrum.be/data" %}
    {% set doc_type = "VSC Tier-1 Data documentation pages" %}
{% else %}
    {% set doc_base = "https://rdm-docs.icts.kuleuven.be/mango" %}
    {% set doc_type = "RDM documentation pages" %}
{% endif %}

<p>You can use the information below to connect to the ManGO platform through various protocols.</p>
<ul class="nav nav-pills">
  <li class="nav-item">
    <a class="nav-link active" data-bs-toggle="pill" href="#irodsClients">iRODS clients</a>
  </li>
  {% if 'desktop-sync' in services %}
  <li class="nav-item">
    <a class="nav-link" data-bs-toggle="pill" href="#owncloud">ownCloud desktop sync</a>
  </li>
  {% endif %}
  {% if 'sftp-server' in services %}
  <li class="nav-item">
    <a class="nav-link" data-bs-toggle="pill" href="#sftp">SFTP</a>
  </li>
  {% endif %}
</ul>
<div class="tab-content">
  <div class="tab-pane container active p-1" id="irodsClients">

    <p class="mt-3">
      {% if '-hpc-' in zone_info['jobid'] %}
      The Tier-1 Data service is reachable over the iRODS protocol using the following connection information.
      {% else %}
      The ManGO platform is reachable over the iRODS protocol using the following connection information.
      {% endif %}
      <i>Note that after June 1st, our iRODS servers will be firewalled. You will either need to connect from a managed laptop, an HPC node, a device in the KU Leuven L- or S-zone,
      or open the web firewall page
      <a href="{{ services['web-firewall']['url'] }}">{{ services['web-firewall']['url']|replace("https://", "") }}</a>,
      before attempting to connect using any of the clients listed below.</i>
    </p>
    
    <table class="table table-sm table-borderless ml-20 mt-3">
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <th>Hostname</th>
        <td>
          {{ zone_info['irods_host'] }}
        </td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <th>Port</th>
        <td>
          {{ zone_info['irods_port'] }}
        </td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <th>Zone</th>
        <td>
          {{ zone_info['irods_zone_name'] }}
        </td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <th>Username</th>
        <td>
          {{ zone_info['irods_user_name'] }}
        </td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <th>Login method</th>
        <td>
          <code>pam_interactive</code>
        </td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
    </table>

      <p class="mt-3 mb-2">
        KU Leuven developed the <code>iron</code> utility to provide user-friendly interaction with your data on the ManGO platform. 
        {% if '-hpc-' in zone_info['jobid'] %}
          Find the <a href="{{ doc_base }}/tier1data/clients/iron.html#installation">installation instructions</a>
          and <a href="{{ doc_base }}/tier1data/clients/iron.html#how-to-use-iron">how to use iron</a> at the {{ doc_type }}.
        {% else %}
          Find the <a href="{{ doc_base }}/clients/iron.html#installation">installation instructions</a>
          and <a href="{{ doc_base }}/clients/iron.html#how-to-use-iron">how to use iron</a> at the {{ doc_type }}.
        {% endif %}
      </p>
      <p>
        Run the snippet below to set up your environment and authenticate using <code>iron</code>:
      </p>
      <div class="code-container ms-2">
        <button class="copy-btn btn btn-sm" onclick="copyToClipboard(this)">
          <i class="bi bi-clipboard"></i> Copy
        </button>
        <pre><code class="user-select-all">iron auth {{ zone_info['irods_user_name'] }} {{ zone_info['irods_zone_name'] }} {{ zone_info['irods_host'] }}</code></pre>
      </div>
      <p>
        If the iRODS session gets expired, simply run <code>iron auth</code> without arguments to reauthenticate to the same iRODS zone. 
        {% if '-hpc-' in zone_info['jobid'] %}
          The created session is also usable by other iRODS clients such as iCommands and PRC.
        {% else %}
          The created session is also usable by other iRODS clients such as <a href="{{ doc_base }}/clients/icommands.html#installation">iCommands</a>, <a href="{{ doc_base }}/clients/python_client.html">PRC</a>.
        {% endif %}
      </p>

      <h6 class="mt-3"><button type="button" class="btn ps-0" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#hpcJobScripts" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="hpcJobScripts">
            <i class="bi bi-chevron-down"></i> How to use in HPC job scripts
          </button></h6>
      <div id="hpcJobScripts" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#irodsClients">
        <p>
          Ensure you have authenticated against the iRODS zone using the command above on the login node. During one month after the initial authentication,
          the following command will be able to refresh the iRODS session without interaction:
        </p>
        <div class="code-container ms-2">
          <button class="copy-btn btn btn-sm" onclick="copyToClipboard(this)">
            <i class="bi bi-clipboard"></i> Copy
          </button>
          <pre><code class="user-select-all">iron auth --non-interactive</code></pre>
        </div>
        <p>
          Put it in the front of your job script. You can control and extend the period in which the iRODS session can be refreshed at 
          {% if 'vsc' in zone_info['irods_user_name'] %}
          <a href="https://auth.vscentrum.be">https://auth.vscentrum.be</a>.
          {% else %}
          <a href="https://mango-auth.icts.kuleuven.be/">https://mango-auth.icts.kuleuven.be/</a>.
          {% endif %}
        </p>
        <p>
          If by any chance the iRODS session cannot be renewed, <code>iron auth ---non-interactive</code> will fail with exit code 1.
        </p>
      </div>

      <h6><button type="button" class="btn ps-0" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#pythonModule" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="pythonModule">
            <i class="bi bi-chevron-down"></i> How to authenticate in python scripts
          </button></h6>
      <div id="pythonModule" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#irodsClients">
        <p>
          Using the <code>iron</code> authentication above prepares the <code>.irods/irods_environment.json</code> and <code>.irods/.irodsA</code> files.
          The python iRODS client can be configured to use these authentication files by putting the following in your code:
        </p>
        <div class="code-container ms-2">
          <button class="copy-btn btn btn-sm" onclick="copyToClipboard(this)">
            <i class="bi bi-clipboard"></i> Copy
          </button>
          <pre><code class="user-select-all">env_file = os.path.expanduser('~/.irods/irods_environment.json')
with iRODSSession(irods_env_file=env_file) as session:
  (...)</code></pre>
        </div>
        <p>
          In some situations it might be beneficial to integrate authentication in a python script, and to prepare the iRODS environment files directly in python.
          For this, ensure python is installed, and install the <code>mango_auth</code> pip module with the command:
        </p>
        <div class="code-container ms-2">
          <button class="copy-btn btn btn-sm" onclick="copyToClipboard(this)">
            <i class="bi bi-clipboard"></i> Copy
          </button>
          <pre><code class="user-select-all">pip install mango_auth</code></pre>
        </div>
        <p>
          To demonstrate that it works correctly, the following command can be used to authenticate against iRODS, instead of <code>iron auth</code>:
        </p>
        <div class="code-container ms-2">
          <button class="copy-btn btn btn-sm" onclick="copyToClipboard(this)">
            <i class="bi bi-clipboard"></i> Copy
          </button>
          <pre><code class="user-select-all">mango_auth {{ zone_info['irods_user_name'] }} {{ zone_info['irods_zone_name'] }} {{ zone_info['irods_host'] }}</code></pre>
        </div>
        <p>
          Once confirmed this works, the following function can be integrated in your python script to do exactly the same without external commands:
        </p>
        <div class="code-container ms-2">
          <button class="copy-btn btn btn-sm" onclick="copyToClipboard(this)">
            <i class="bi bi-clipboard"></i> Copy
          </button>
          <pre><code class="user-select-all">from mango_auth import iinit
iinit("{{ zone_info['irods_user_name'] }}", "{{ zone_info['irods_zone_name'] }}", "{{ zone_info['irods_host'] }}")

env_file = os.path.expanduser('~/.irods/irods_environment.json')
with iRODSSession(irods_env_file=env_file) as session:
  (...)</code></pre>
        </div>
      </div>

      <h6><button type="button" class="btn ps-0" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#linuxPamInteractive" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="linuxPamInteractive">
            <i class="bi bi-chevron-down"></i> With iCommands only for Linux operating systems
          </button></h6>
      <div id="linuxPamInteractive" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#irodsClients">
        <p>
          If the <code>iron</code> command is not available, it is also possible to authenticate with iCommands only on Linux operating systems.
          Make sure that your iRODS icommands installation is 5.0.0 or above and includes the <code>irods-auth-plugin-pam-interactive-client</code> package.
          Run the snippet below to configure an iRODS client under Linux.
        </p>
        <div class="code-container ms-2">
          <button class="copy-btn btn btn-sm" onclick="copyToClipboard(this)">
            <i class="bi bi-clipboard"></i> Copy
          </button>
          <pre><code class="user-select-all">mkdir -p ~/.irods
cat > ~/.irods/irods_environment.json <<'EOF'
{{ setup_json }}
EOF
iinit --ttl 168 && echo You are now authenticated to iRODS.
</code></pre>
        </div>
        <p>
          The iRODS session remains valid for one week. Run <code>iinit --ttl 168</code> again to refresh.
          In contrast to authentication with <code>iron</code>, a login URL will be shown every time.
        </p>
      </div>

      <h6><button type="button" class="btn ps-0" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#otherApplications" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="otherApplications">
            <i class="bi bi-chevron-down"></i> Authentication in other iRODS applications
          </button></h6>
      <div id="otherApplications" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#irodsClients">
        <p>
          In principal, any existing iRODS tool might be used to connect to the ManGO zones, provided it supports TLS encryption and the <code>pam_interactive</code> authentication scheme, although your mileage may vary.
        </p>
        <p>
          Consult the <a href="{% if '-hpc-' in zone_info['jobid'] %}{{ doc_base }}/tier1data/clients.html{% else %}{{ doc_base }}/clients.html{% endif %}">client list at the {{ doc_type }}</a> to check which clients we actively support.
        </p>
      </div>
    
      {% if 'hpc-irods-setup-zone' in info %}
      <h6><button type="button" class="btn ps-0" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#linuxHPC" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="linuxHPC">
            <i class="bi bi-chevron-down"></i> Deprecated: The irods-setup command on HPC infrastructure
          </button></h6>
      <div id="linuxHPC" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#irodsClients">
        <p>
          <i>This method is deprecrated and will stop working on April 1st, 2026.</i>
        </p>
        <p>
          On the HPC tier1 or tier2 clusters in Leuven, run the snippet below to
          configure an iRODS client. The iRODS session itself will last for a
          week, afterwards repeat the command.
        </p>
        <div class="code-container ms-2">
          <pre><code>irods-setup --zone {{ info['hpc-irods-setup-zone'] }} | bash</code></pre>
        </div>
        <p>
          From other HPC clusters in Flanders, you can run
          <code class="user-select-all">ssh login.hpc.kuleuven.be irods-setup --zone
            {{ info['hpc-irods-setup-zone'] }} | bash</code>. If this command through ssh does not work, please run it without
          <code>| bash</code> to troubleshoot.
        </p>
      </div>
      {% endif %}
    </div>

    {% if 'desktop-sync' in services %}
    <div class="tab-pane container fade p-1" id="owncloud">
      <p class="mt-3">
        The ownCloud desktop sync application can be used to synchorize an iRODS folder to your local workstation.

        See the instructions below or the <a href="{% if '-hpc-' in zone_info['jobid'] %}{{ doc_base }}{% else %}{{ doc_base }}/clients/owncloud.html{% endif %}">{{ doc_type }}</a> for more detailed information.
      </p>
      <p>
        <i>The use of ownCloud is currently in an open pilot phase. Please report any feedback to the RDM team.</i>
      </p>
      <ol>
        <li>Ensure the ownCloud desktop client for Windows or Linux is installed via your local IT-support, or via the installation instructions at <a href="https://owncloud.com/desktop-app">https://owncloud.com/desktop-app</a>.</li>
        <li>Open ownCloud and click on "Add account". On the box to provide your server's address, enter a URL:
          <div class="code-container ms-2 mt-2">
            <button class="copy-btn btn btn-sm" onclick="copyToClipboard(this)">
              <i class="bi bi-clipboard"></i> Copy
            </button>
            <pre><code class="user-select-all">{{ services['desktop-sync']['url'] }}</code></pre>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li>Click on "Open Browser" to log in to ownCloud. To grant privileges to ownCloud click on "Agree and continue to the application".</li>
        <li>In the client, you get "You're all set!" message and there is a checkbox to select advanced configuration. <strong>Check the "Advanced configuration" box.</strong></li>
        <li>Additional options on the configuration show up. Options under advanced configuration Select "Configure synchronization manually" to manually determine what is synced, otherwise you pull-in all the files you have access to.</li>
        <li>Pick a local folder on your computer to sync. Navigate to the ManGO Project you want to synchronize locally.</li>
        <li>Keep checked the option to "Use virtual files instead of downloading content manually" and click on "Add sync connection".</li>
      </ol>
    </div>
    {% endif %}

    {% if 'sftp-server' in services %}
    <div class="tab-pane container fade p-1" id="sftp">
      <p class="mt-3">
        You can also use SFTP to connect to iRODS and use programs such as Filezilla, WinSCP or <code>lftp</code>.
        It is a file transfer protocol on top of SSH and SSH certificates are used for authentication.
      </p>
      <p>
        <i>Note that after June 1st, the SFTP service will be firewalled. You will either need to connect from a managed laptop, an HPC node, a device in the KU Leuven L- or S-zone,
        or to open the web firewall page 
        <a href="{{ services['web-firewall']['url'] }}">{{ services['web-firewall']['url']|replace("https://", "") }}</a>,
        before attempting to connect.</i>
      </p>
      <ol>
        {% if '-hpc-' in zone_info['jobid'] %}
          <li>
            You need to run an <code>ssh-agent</code> capable of handling SSH certificates.
            <br />
            For Windows, <a href="https://www.chiark.greenend.org.uk/~sgtatham/putty/latest.html">Pageant 0.78</a> or above can be used.
            For Linux, the standard OpenSSH agent will work.
          </li>
          <li>
            Connect with e.g. Putty to <code>firewall.vscentrum.be</code> with agent forwarding enabled.
            After having successfully connected, an SSH certificate should be injected in your forwarded agent.
          </li>
        {% else %}
          <li>
            Install <a href="https://admin.kuleuven.be/icts/services/ssh-cert">certagent or kmk</a> on your local machine
            and use it to retrieve an SSH certificate.
          </li>
        {% endif %}
        <li>
          Open FileZilla or WinSCP, and connect using the following information:
          <dl class="mx-auto ml-20 mt-3">
            <dt>Hostname</dt>
            <dd>
              {{ services['sftp-server']['url']|replace("sftp://", "") }}
            </dd>
            <dt>Port</dt>
            <dd>
              22
            </dd>
            <dt>Username</dt>
            <dd>
              {{ zone_info['irods_user_name'] }}
            </dd>
            <dt>Password</dt>
            <dd>
              Leave empty. For FileZilla set 'Authentication type' to 'Interactive'.
            </dd>
          </dl>
          Or use <code>lftp -u {{ zone_info['irods_user_name'] }}, {{ services['sftp-server']['url'] }}</code>.
        </li>
      </ol>
    </div>
    {% endif %}
  </div>